      ro: "Clava Cairns este un complex de morminte din epoca bronzului lângă Culloden, Scoția. Este format din trei movile de piatră (cairns) și un cerc de pietre. Datează din jurul anului 2000 î.Hr. Alinierea mormintelor indică cunoștințe astronomice. Situl este liber accesibil, administrat de Historic Environment Scotland. Săpăturile au început în secolul al XIX-lea. Numele 'Clava' provine din gaelică.",
      en: "Clava Cairns is a Bronze Age burial complex located near Culloden in the Scottish Highlands. It comprises three well-preserved passage graves (cairns) and standing stone circles, dating from around 2000 BC. The site shows careful alignment with the midwinter sunset, indicating astronomical significance. The largest cairn, the Balnuaran of Clava, has a diameter of 17 metres. The site was first excavated in 1822 by James Logan. It is a scheduled monument and managed by Historic Environment Scotland. Clava Cairns is a popular destination for those interested in prehistoric Britain and is also linked to the nearby Culloden Battlefield.",
